 none; padding: 0;">As we've learned in earlier lessons, the entire dispute=
 process is automated. Rarely are there human eyes that read your letters. =
Your disputes are broken down into a two digit code. So, if the computer no=
tices a mismatch in the address ID then you are more likely to get the acco=
unt over to an actual person, sent through the proper verification process =
or even removed. The same is true for a name change. If the client's name h=
as been legally changed and they've applied for credit under their new name=
 and the name is reporting on the credit report or if they can provide proo=
f of the name change and dispute an account attached to their previous=0Ana=
me, you are more likely to get the derogatory information attached to the o=
ld name off the report.</div>=0A<div style=3D"margin: 0 8.15pt 0 0; outline=
: none; padding: 0;"><br>When attempting to remove addresses from the repor=
t, there are a few angles you can take. We'll discuss one here. If your cli=
ent would like to change their current address to an address that is not on=
 the report, you can ask the client if they have a relative with the same l=
ast name who's address they don't mind their mail from the bureaus being de=
livered to. In your update letter you could say that the client is currentl=
y residing with their cousin or uncle and use their cousin=E2=80=99s or unc=
le=E2=80=99s utility bill as proof of address, then request all other addre=
sses reporting be removed since they are not current and are outdated. Beca=
use their last names match, it=E2=80=99s easy to believe that the updated a=
ddress may be associated with the consumer, just like how a utility bill wi=
ll typically only have one name, but a married couple may be living in that=
 home. If you try this on a client, please remember to=0Ainform them that t=
heir mail from the bureaus will go to that relative's address.<br><br>If th=
ey don't want to send mail to a relative's address, a business address, a c=
ustomized UPS address or PO Box can work as long as they have proof of the =
address with their name or someone of the same last name. <br></div>=0A<div=
 style=3D"margin: 0 8.15pt 0 5pt; outline: none; padding: 0;"><br></div>=0A=
